  "answer": "I found no past ticket that reports this problem. The nearest one is PowerToys#48725, where a context-item shortcut navigates twice. Its cause is different. Both CommandBar and ContextMenu handle the same TryCommandKeybindingMessage. Your report is about LocalKeyboardListener's keyboard hook treating HC_NOREMOVE peeks as key events. No archived ticket mentions that. Treat this as a new bug. The fix you propose is to process only HC_ACTION (nCode == 0) notifications in the hook and to ignore HC_NOREMOVE. To help maintainers, please add reproduction steps, the shortcut that fires twice, and the actual behavior to the ticket."
 },
